Fable helped explain how the effects work, and watching the demos and experimenting with them is very satisfying.

@johnowhitaker is making a drawing app inspired by his nature journal style, where watercolor wash dynamics mean you can't be too precious about every line. He encourages others to give it a try.

The linked resources include an explanation of how the inkwash effect works and the GitHub repository for the pen-and-ink with living water drawing app.

Delightful article.

@Moultano: "I spent the last month obsessed with finding colors that can't be displayed on a conventional screen. This is what I found."

An atlas of the vibrance of the real world.
